<title>PORTUGAL: Banco Mello sees improving results by 2000.</title>
<headline>Banco Mello sees improving results by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese bank Banco Mello Comercial expects a sharp improvement in its results by the end of the century and will benefit from a tax credit of 36 billion escudos, the president of its executive board said.</p>
<p>&quot;By the end of the century we will report distinguished results,&quot; Francisco Lacerda said during the presentation of the bank's 1996 results. He gave no precise forecasts.</p>
<p>Banco Mello posted a 1996 net profit of 0.5 billion escudos, compared with losses of 1.8 billion escudos in 1995.</p>
<p>The tax credit was owed to Banco Mello following a five-year period of losses.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
